{% endif %}## Install

```sh
curl -fsSLo ~/.config/ironbar/acid-acetic.css \
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/acid-theme/ironbar/main/acid-acetic.css
```

Import it at the top of `~/.config/ironbar/style.css`, so a later definition
can override it:

```css
@import url("acid-acetic.css");

#bar {
    background-color: @base;
    color: @text;
}

popover > contents {
    color: @text;
    background-color: @base;
    border: 1px solid @surface1;
}
```

Popups are GTK popovers, so the widgets inside them (buttons, sliders, the
calendar) keep your GTK theme's colours until a rule names them.

GTK reports no error for a colour name it does not know, so a misspelt role
leaves that widget unstyled.

